01:58:49.809 --> 01:58:53.449
So before we start reading this view model,
I just wanted to mention a couple of things

01:58:53.449 --> 01:58:54.449
here.

01:58:54.449 --> 01:58:58.269
As discussed in the introduction for this
particular section, I didn't actually want

01:58:58.269 --> 01:59:03.800
to use any of the jetpack libraries to achieve
a publisher subscriber relationship between

01:59:03.800 --> 01:59:05.309
the view model and the view.

01:59:05.309 --> 01:59:10.309
Now, it turns out that that publisher, subscriber
relationship or pattern is actually quite

01:59:10.309 --> 01:59:12.309
easy to implement.

01:59:12.309 --> 01:59:17.169
But in this case, I actually found it simpler
to just use kotlin function types to achieve

01:59:17.169 --> 01:59:21.940
what I would call a poor person's publisher,
subscriber pattern or observer pattern.

01:59:21.940 --> 01:59:25.679
So this really means something simple in practice,
although it might look kind of complicated

01:59:25.679 --> 01:59:29.190
for those who aren't really familiar with
working with function types.

01:59:29.190 --> 01:59:33.429
Our view model will possess these nullable
function type references.

01:59:33.429 --> 01:59:38.099
As we'll see in a moment, what we can do is
